# Expected artifact type: key (hardcoded-secret, entropy + config layers)
# Expected Exposure = Internal.
# NOTE (found while building this fixture): scanner/pipeline.py's own docstring lists
# '.env' as a protected internal file type, but engine.js's isInternalFileType() list
# does NOT include '.env' (only .db/.sqlite/.sqlite3 + a set of folder names). It still
# ends up Internal here via the "no signals triggered -> default Internal" fallback,
# NOT via the fast-path rule — so it's correct today, but only by coincidence. If a
# future .env line ever contains a route-like token, it would no longer be protected.
# Worth adding '.env' to engine.js's isInternalFileType list explicitly.
